{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.058354Z","id":"c77c0394c086d807772f6441102c3ff94e064baf6b44658b4202fd6529dfe544","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:496-503, record f3b6a110.\n\nIdentity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":651},"end":{"line":658},"content_hash":"e518245782ac10f00f2b65f20d7c675055af73af8c7fb3c52ec0df3ab6eb723b"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"c685963278cbdc55e58d7e3b5086c00a8cb08e9f8adff1b4436ded2e1c52847e","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/viewer.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.090839Z","id":"15bc103c93c1b4a3c2bda1413b656e7a055738a035c8ec128981900d0620448b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/viewer.rs:106-121, record 96c44912.\n\nA Clax-Grant caller writing a thread or a comment without author_kind agent is attributed to its grant's person (author_public_id, display name), as the token's agents are to the owner. Storing it as an agent comment with its session would show it as the agent's in the shell, but a thread's first comment is a viewer comment (NewThread) and a viewer comment forwards the thread, so the semantics would change. Authorship, which the filter needs, is right either way.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"e1def51929c14fd1c99fd4ce1be5af13d57093d7b469bb09c77918167b711764"},"summary":"A person's agent's viewer-kind comment is stored as its person's viewer comment, not as an agent comment","supersedes":"ca958e058f0cec86571d1f0f99a56994639f6be29eef5489eaaf390a72438e8d","tags":["revisit:when the shell shows which agent wrote a person's comment","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.164562Z","id":"40bb34fbfb0c82746eb90428ba529762f6b578573f9a1f5a98a757194ce1946e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:150-152, record 10f82840.\n\nArtifactsFork declares (clax-artifacts, read), so the Agent extractor answers a person's agent lacking read 403 not_permitted, as every agent read route does (GET /api/artifacts/<aid> too), while a hosted member's browser gets 404 from the member gate and a local connected person's browser 404 from routes/artifacts.rs fork_refusal. Tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs a_member_forks_what_they_may_read_into_their_own_artifact (404), api_forks.rs (404 for a local person).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"84ab821874e5fae80fe4de0740363b3be77453a82a1cb90633dc4a0b975bfed8"},"summary":"A person's agent without read on the source is refused fork with 403 not_permitted, a person's browser with 404","tags":["forks","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.164659Z","id":"1bee178a21d78d83b5f7533b8531b370f7aedd3c5ef8f6f0e812cd338b850bc5","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:531-531, record 077718a7.\n\napi_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":531},"end":{"line":531},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","tags":["people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.164727Z","id":"fcbec7b26337f525b2b99f623b948f633709fcafeb934e263a9ecca94f7158c3","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:1131-1131, record da9f1184.\n\nEvery handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":1131},"end":{"line":1131},"content_hash":"0084401cde97b2431fc0a50fda577f15da02d5950c956b6bd243c5b7d069ce7d"},"summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.164785Z","id":"8ca5839efcfee4c03e8834d1a2c21c5c8a0367be4044bb3985b7576eac971cfe","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/audit.rs:333-342, record c54728e1.\n\nThe extractor's own job costs one interactive round trip before the handler's. Measured with a scratch test against TestServer (debug build, 4 runtime workers, 300-400 sequential requests, three rounds): GET /api/_test/audit/ctx, which is only the extraction, p50 201-227 us against /healthz 144-157 us at idle (about 60 us per job); with 8 clients looping on GET /api/viewers/me, a one-job route at p50 411-420 us, p95 557-566 us, and the extraction alone p50 426-445 us, p95 572-1316 us, so each audited write pays about one more queue wait. Agent tool calls also add one writer transaction for tool.call and, under Claude Code, one for tool.call_id, read-only tools and each wait_for_feedback included. The perf gates passed on unchanged budgets (docs/verification.md §10). Not fixed in the branch's final round: 23 handlers in seven route modules (artifacts, assets, docs, feedback, live, sites, threads, plus the live refile context) take AuditCtx, each with its own job structure, so moving the resolve into their jobs is a change to every audited route rather than a cheap one.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":333},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"fde9f6c59006fc734d792edc237fec3e153f53108171e787e2ff1539a90cf319"},"suggested_fix":"Take DeferredAudit in the handlers and resolve it inside the handler's own store job, as the session routes already do with for_session.","summary":"Every request that records an event now takes two interactive store jobs: the AuditCtx extractor resolves the actor in its own store_call before the handler's","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.165055Z","id":"a5c04cf14514c3880ce8df7d155e983784e5af984cc3cd3b0f047f73bf85a0b2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs:153-171, record 36bf936e.\n\nis_grant_request includes Bearer cxa_…, and verify_layer admits it wherever a route's need! admits grants, so a script holding an agent token can call the API directly with the same rights its MCP tools have. The prototype (hosted/src/mcp/server.ts) took the token only at /mcp. The rights are identical either way; restricting it to in-process requests from the adapter would need a marker the loopback sets.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"e6eb9b5cd97f310ac94ca698005b960357df7ef98121b5cc7bb8c8f5000f777c"},"summary":"An agent token is an agent credential on every route a grant may reach, not only through the MCP adapter","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.165447Z","id":"803a76f17d1f5c144620a00c787d779589f1f454f10994004c2260663a9d1e1b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs:23-31, record 668f8f3a.\n\nhosted/src/git/tokens.ts refused write tokens to anyone but the owner (403 owner_only) because there every pushed commit was credited to the owner. Here a push is recorded as a version published by the token's holder (clax_core::store::pushes, Store::standing rechecks the pusher's update right at record time), so pushing is publishing and the route asks for the same right a publish does: under clax:collaborator that is the person's own artifacts, under clax:full every artifact. The alternative is owner and owner's agents only (Caller::Owner / OwnerAgent), refusing every person's write token.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:4d4f7fb20f8f80c4a82d838442bf23c8ef0dfbfb","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"0e98812e150e2b9f3b12d9a5ac43ff8060532f49329002c749240d788fffbe66"},"summary":"A write token needs clax-artifacts update (the publish right), not the prototype's owner-only push","tags":["status:needs-decision","revisit:a person with update rights should not be able to push","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.165526Z","id":"86481da4da4869896caa807e0d37b6b17d95fa13dd8531bf8d2b86d11c3ef387","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs:532-543, record 0caf9cae.\n\nAsker::Link has no reader (Asker::reader is None, as for people), so check_history does not run for it: no 503 while pushed commits wait (clax_core::store::pushes), and Store::repo_history's refused_pushers' commits stay reachable from main. A member's clone carries the same, but a link reaches anyone who has it. Narrowing would need a host that serves only version tags to link tokens.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4d4f7fb20f8f80c4a82d838442bf23c8ef0dfbfb","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":324},"content_hash":"0d09c7764a8f34cc69851914496389ab09377c6c3b88d93e1f64ff0a1f6de19e"},"summary":"A page link's read token clones main whole: pushed commits not yet recorded as versions, and refused pushes left on main, reach whoever holds the link, though the page shows them only its versions","tags":["git","hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.165571Z","id":"98af064f2c7a184426f074a7ff2cd598194dd3b2795ab7e38810ded4cf168dad","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs:730-750, record c906a641.\n\nA pasted command lands in the shell's history with the token, and while git runs any user of the machine can read its -c argument in the process list. The GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0/GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 form (what jj_clone_command and the jj commands use) keeps it out of other users' process list but not out of the history, and does not work as pasted in PowerShell or cmd; a credential helper given inline (-c credential.helper=...) is on the command line the same way. Keeping it out of the history needs two steps (read the token into a variable, then run the command with it), which a one-paste flow does not have. docs/contract.md 'Git remotes' states the trade; the tokens' lives (3600 s, 900 s for agents) bound it.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:4d4f7fb20f8f80c4a82d838442bf23c8ef0dfbfb","span":{"start":{"line":511},"end":{"line":531},"content_hash":"6b54dbed5895c129171356cda07b70b28b4862cb13ea6c3e866d6a1beb86530f"},"summary":"The commands carry the token on git's command line (-c http.extraHeader), as the hosted spec's section 9 and hosted/src/git/commands.ts do, not in the environment or a credential helper","tags":["security","revisit:shared multi-user machines are a target, or the dialog grows a two-step flow","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.165612Z","id":"6531e06a2d4417884ec020f91d1f78d5f77e0386b9f536c305c91c0e5b617665","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs:948-979, record 27341258.\n\nrecheck asks the host for every live held token (RepoDO token/held on the Worker) and, per token, builds a Visibility and reads Store::repo_history (the artifact's and its lineage's versions and refused pushers). listen runs it after every Version, ArtifactDeleted, People and Agents event burst; settle_layer before answering a request that moved the generation; and listen once when a server is built (each Durable Object wake). Fine for a handful of tokens; with many, a recheck per artifact and a per-reader Visibility cache would bound it.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4d4f7fb20f8f80c4a82d838442bf23c8ef0dfbfb","span":{"start":{"line":729},"end":{"line":760},"content_hash":"b17df665b58dc5c49d825e15cc8d73520f3048d38ecd43a929bfefa2ebed202b"},"summary":"A recheck lists every held token from the host and walks each one's repository history: run on every relevant event, every request that moves the visibility generation, and every server built anew","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.185885Z","id":"930a2cdfdfee1ac179d6d28c701931c7cda59a419ca69a2e84bfa48c27d7b68f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:197-200, record ed323928.\n\nLimits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","span":{"start":{"line":194},"end":{"line":197},"content_hash":"c3d9cee2df2daa7466bec6f2d7785f46a526e8ffaae9cfc54cec9c2e75b2fe50"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.185981Z","id":"ad4d8d8c97b30ea324cdbd7218826481a8ddbad720b28cae710d7325b0f14f3a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:542-544, record 16ca7740.\n\ncontent_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","span":{"start":{"line":539},"end":{"line":541},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.186049Z","id":"2b006cc0e57d1bd9a98cc8d7e7d29b29e8ed2b344bd59cf97af640eb110821f3","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:669-674, record 6b80c3e5.\n\nThe gate could require /c/<aid>/draft/k/<content key of the base version>/<agent>/<token>/…, so a draft URL is also bound to a key the daemon derives. Not taken: the draft token is already 128 random bits minted per revision (clax_core::drafts::new_token), handed only to people who may read the artifact, and it expires with the revision, which a content key never does; a second key adds a path segment the shell's draftSrc (web/shell/src/view/draft-model.ts) and the artifact host rewrite (crates/clax-server/src/host.rs) would carry for no capability the token lacks.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","span":{"start":{"line":666},"end":{"line":671},"content_hash":"1784c2024ba3d1b89730649afd8e4da2b8bb437c88275427391e1e49fcc54dd8"},"summary":"Draft URLs keyed by the version's content key as well as the draft token","tags":["hosted","drafts","revisit:a draft token is logged, persisted or handed to anyone who may not read the artifact","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.186110Z","id":"63ce5763c0196d3bba5e418b059982564b9fe0d3069fcdf8a0d21bdcd088927e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:933-937, record a625cb63.\n\nmember_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","span":{"start":{"line":930},"end":{"line":934},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.186167Z","id":"75c0506b253ac283a35c6618578644946e0d8b609fd3cf300c2af90ef381043f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1013-1013, record bffc5d23.\n\nmember_gate drops `gallery` from such a person's subscriptions because gallery events (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes, project) carry every artifact's titles and thread summaries; their gallery refreshes on load only.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","span":{"start":{"line":1010},"end":{"line":1010},"content_hash":"9471bb31c6d4f0b2d71a36f6b8d1a2337a69bc2c12c507c336dbacf34ac7fdc2"},"suggested_fix":"Gate gallery items per subscriber by artifact (a read filter fixed at subscribe time) instead of dropping the topic.","summary":"A person whose rights do not read every artifact gets no gallery stream topic, so their gallery does not update live","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.186227Z","id":"4f449f18717d16fa8462adf699146a5355235181cab5bd661d6d2cd09923b033","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1181-1183, record 5d1ab740.\n\nThe prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","span":{"start":{"line":1178},"end":{"line":1180},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.186285Z","id":"ddaee3f9dbacd808b879f2923a80d54cbfe33c1412ad1171fdad9b4e6608e4e6","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1607-1615, record 5be58509.\n\nPUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","span":{"start":{"line":1604},"end":{"line":1612},"content_hash":"d6db51fbfe5931fb0d00605685ea2de5cccafa046c6c89f623e78fc68fb20aa2"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.212048Z","id":"200d4d60fab2ffe95e394bc9fec4d4e90f3b6be748788470629851d0f66cf5c1","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:28-29, record 51900b96.\n\nA LAN viewer (the clax_viewer cookie) can create viewers, threads, comments, sends and db documents without limit. Decision needed: add rate limits for LAN writes, and at what rates.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"b1af0cd8867a4f59d11928f5b6bc91ec050b31c1c0962ba44425b10f430d2c0c"},"summary":"LAN viewers' writes have no rate limit","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.212109Z","id":"b38524341e82a3ea019df5cbc1b1bbfb67fc80903d6680738695fe760274d0de","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:654-661, record 3f88c0a6.\n\nIdentity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":654},"end":{"line":661},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.844469Z","id":"66ee3d55f637a69b899684765c1c986fa2a79fec7987528ee094b61d38d732d4","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs:403-424, record 7aa11f30.\n\ncrate::seats::subscribe (called by POST /api/stream/<id>, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update) takes the artifact's seat for connection stream:<id> when the stream holds none of its live topics yet. If two calls add live topics of the same artifact at once and one then fails (TooMany, Hidden), its rollback leaves the seat the other call's topics rely on. The shell's hub sends one change at a time per stream, so this needs a hand-made client.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3079e4aa12ba3d7b1a5565f968fcac279fe986b5","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":174},"content_hash":"4c1d002bb08b1e78d10906ff498e81fd66cd9f8f4590b4773cb4c6d540bb79bd"},"summary":"Two concurrent subscription changes of one stream can leave it on an artifact's live topics without its seat","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/socket_caps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.844666Z","id":"49249c3c5d999900f56c0b5dfe5246c98731877939e2790aa8e952278e750a12","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/socket_caps.rs:11-13, record b4bd61b2.\n\nSocketClient::of_request answers no keys without [hosted], so SocketCaps::admit always admits there: the realtime load gate (scripts/perf-clients.py) drives thousands of /api/stream connections from one address. A LAN viewer of a daemon bound beyond loopback is as unbounded as before (see also record 51900b96 on LAN viewers' writes). Capping LAN viewers by address while exempting loopback and the token would close it.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:bb36b7f4b2d63f5e6de02e255d0e67b8e32875fb","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":13},"content_hash":"fcc46cbaa0c5dcf6b1417b3b8271de27f1e7468bb5695a3c027b5d5b3f968b41"},"summary":"A local daemon caps no client's streams or sockets: a LAN viewer may open any number","tags":["security","resource","streams","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/viewer.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.844829Z","id":"29e9b7574a064936b94afb460ed2ed08221353af4802440403d1377126095bdc","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/viewer.rs:124-139, record dd6eeef9.\n\nA Clax-Grant caller writing a thread or a comment without author_kind agent is attributed to its grant's person (author_public_id, display name), as the token's agents are to the owner. Storing it as an agent comment with its session would show it as the agent's in the shell, but a thread's first comment is a viewer comment (NewThread) and a viewer comment forwards the thread, so the semantics would change. Authorship, which the filter needs, is right either way.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"83ee2c4a800f2125d8a2bab39db59a095b257bef4fe8d7cf0c04be3b50037d7d"},"summary":"A person's agent's viewer-kind comment is stored as its person's viewer comment, not as an agent comment","tags":["revisit:when the shell shows which agent wrote a person's comment","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.519645Z","id":"d1fe6a4c43a948c12f9f60c79951d2943846d90e046695b6e60bee21ff54caa9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8ca5839efcfee4c03e8834d1a2c21c5c8a0367be4044bb3985b7576eac971cfe","summary":"Narrowed, not fixed: b24b98e0 folds the feedback poll's audit context (audit::session_ctx) into its first view's store call and a person's agent's path-artifact right into the caller's own store call, so a person's agent's poll takes three store jobs before answering (four before) and its threads read two (three before). The AuditCtx extractor this record names is unchanged in the 23 audited handlers.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.537883Z","id":"09b0c700b63352e4a3f5d3c44adbc7ac0da30de2385af9b11981fb80e1193103","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a5c04cf14514c3880ce8df7d155e983784e5af984cc3cd3b0f047f73bf85a0b2","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.593239Z","id":"f0428729c3980538fe2a36e49d3f0be6dc4ecd2f9590acef73f425ba828ce820","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"803a76f17d1f5c144620a00c787d779589f1f454f10994004c2260663a9d1e1b","summary":"Since 4f1f7191 this holds only where the host names pushers (GitRemotes::names_pushers): with REPO_STORE=artifacts a push is recorded as the owner's, so there write tokens go to the owner and the owner's agents alone (403 push_unattributed), as the prototype's owner_only did. The decision this record asks for stands for the stand-in.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.593399Z","id":"60454d4bdf050cbe38f31df8a4460397fc4841ccfb2cf908e993f32096977642","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"803a76f17d1f5c144620a00c787d779589f1f454f10994004c2260663a9d1e1b","summary":"The owner's decision: 'Anyone with update' — a write token needs clax-artifacts update at the artifact, the right a publish needs, as implemented here. With the exception the review added (4f1f7191): where the host cannot name pushers (GitRemotes::names_pushers false, Cloudflare Artifacts) write tokens stay owner-only (403 push_unattributed) until pushers can be attributed.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.666825Z","id":"7331a3c379309244445ec2b256871c02485f5495c7c84da3d270afe553a893b6","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"930a2cdfdfee1ac179d6d28c701931c7cda59a419ca69a2e84bfa48c27d7b68f","summary":"On the Worker the limits live in the instance object's memory: one instance object serves every client, so they are counted per site, and they reset at every wake or eviction as at a daemon restart.","tags":["worker","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.666974Z","id":"409e58994e6dba59659b90fa5ce2715b29b076d7c69a6271d635d8e3d4c8d5fd","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"930a2cdfdfee1ac179d6d28c701931c7cda59a419ca69a2e84bfa48c27d7b68f","summary":"The device sign-in limits (Attempt::Device, Attempt::DevicePoll) are counted in the same in-memory Limits; the store bounds what survives a restart: codes expire after 600 s, at most 1,000 wait at once (crates/clax-core/src/store/device.rs MAX_PENDING_DEVICES), and polls are slowed by polled_at on the store clock","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.685396Z","id":"8ad881599b3f8d25587726d2ab429dfefcd72642dc39ce4bc60b46e5cb906116","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ad4d8d8c97b30ea324cdbd7218826481a8ddbad720b28cae710d7325b0f14f3a","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.685545Z","id":"3c40a2c152a25f33d840df4fa35048ce387b41ae07c8132617132ee7968b5585","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ad4d8d8c97b30ea324cdbd7218826481a8ddbad720b28cae710d7325b0f14f3a","summary":"Per-artifact shares (crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs) have the same gap: a person whose share is removed keeps reading every version whose keyed content address they already saw, though the artifact's routes answer them 404.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.685687Z","id":"f9082fa616c31b18c4a24fcdff93820fdbdea182b52d789e42929ca7a63e4a31","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ad4d8d8c97b30ea324cdbd7218826481a8ddbad720b28cae710d7325b0f14f3a","summary":"A clip's keyed address (/_clip/<aid>/<tid>?k=<key>, clip_key and clip_link) has the same property: an agent that was shown it keeps reading the clip after it loses the right or the clip becomes withheld, until the thread is deleted.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.741336Z","id":"9f32dce1ed2bee0b2700e48b7f7bae74445cee66c19e0a49d1921a32b0b7008a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"75c0506b253ac283a35c6618578644946e0d8b609fd3cf300c2af90ef381043f","summary":"Since hosted invites give their person their own space (crates/clax-server/src/routes/grants.rs create_invite), every invited person and every GitHub member is such a person: an artifact shared with them appears in their gallery on reload, not live.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
