{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:08.064845Z","id":"20a84754071b07b561f473443ad3b133f6dd295c43d7fef09b0b213836536fd0","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:565-591, record 4585fb7a.\n\nThe keyed address is an HMAC of <aid>/<tid> (clip_key), not a hash of the PNG: a thread's clip is written once and never changes for that (artifact, thread) pair (a move to another artifact makes a new pair, crates/clax-core/src/store/site.rs put_clip), so the address is immutable without reading every clip to hash it for a listing. Clips stay stored once per thread (ContentStore::put_clip). The hosted shell still loads clip_url (GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads/<tid>/clip, credentialed, Cache-Control private, max-age=3600); thread views carry clip_link only for agents (VisFor::of in crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs). Pointing the shell's <img> at the keyed address would make one cacheable URL for both, and needs browser verification of the hosted shell.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:562:588 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:644:668: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":650},"end":{"line":674},"content_hash":"088272ca3a5d64f436e23082a73f135e24cf3f92181ed8b2d2f98437ed5bb7a0"},"summary":"Key a clip's address by its content hash, and have the hosted shell load clips from it","supersedes":"9c5cbb8e87bcdf5999ec013f99796eab3473d513add3645812f9d1ec0f3de44f","tags":["hosted","revisit:hosted shell clip loads show in the time-to-usable budget, or a clip's bytes may change for its thread","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:09.810739Z","id":"9e59786e305b782dbf52fbe99a1e02f90cc30313ce4eb8ffe055a5d1fe2b0dad","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:197-200, record ed323928.\n\nLimits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":227},"content_hash":"e773e1438242b272aff7abb4426e25b6868af8c1d503cc1f0ab28083fc52603f"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"8c35f7f60d9c7a4f5e06ee02ea6cf62451699b2dc723b766beda390d0033a3d3","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:09.883742Z","id":"62e7dd55e7885636aebcd2c52588a6d1ef567b4efb987797f3426fd9093491e1","body":{"detail":"owners_people_view removes from each access object the locations naming artifacts out of the owner's reach and counts them in hidden_locations (tested by api_hosted::the_owners_people_names_no_page_of_another_person). PUT /api/people/<pid>/rights (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs set_rights) replaces a person's rights with the value sent, and the shell (web/shell/src/people) builds that value from what People showed, so the owner re-saving a person's rights drops the hidden locations. Those include artifact IDs of the person's own pages, which are within the person's reach and do grant there (a location naming another person's artifact has no effect on hosted). Raises are per granter and narrowings are the person's own, so only a person's rights round-trip this way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":902},"end":{"line":945},"content_hash":"41294579380e6815f5488408bfbf51e56ec211a988309954a468461835e3bf45"},"suggested_fix":"On hosted, have set_rights keep the stored locations out of the owner's reach when it replaces a person's rights (the owner cannot see them, so cannot mean to drop them), or refuse a value that would drop them.","summary":"A rights value People shows the owner on hosted leaves out hidden locations, so an edit built from it drops them","supersedes":"9590dc3b02705592ffc5f9e19ff47369fb86e057f3a726324062cd21a6aaf35e","tags":["hosted","people","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:09.960320Z","id":"bdea98c5e26a0104439c08c862150647ce3289ddcb0236cca175cf77cfb73cfb","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:933-937, record a625cb63.\n\nmember_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:930:934 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1263:1267: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1101},"end":{"line":1105},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"b61447304fa606524cab6f9ba3e192700ba08e4d2c43420c037aaf041beedaa1","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:10.039620Z","id":"9ddc9cd4c117c62ef3ce99e56f68a6a80de8ee159178ef8d473b9bce992beb50","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1181-1183, record 5d1ab740.\n\nThe prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1178:1180 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1499:1501: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1361},"end":{"line":1363},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"6a07d4395a7f4e16d3221ec53ed8d3c9d99a309ad3d52511f5c701885e36fc87","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:10.113403Z","id":"a479d008261feb72aa0030afe8b0fd4dc7117f2008c5617d3b11588cf815c7cf","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1607-1615, record 5be58509.\n\nPUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1604:1612 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1970:1978: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1845},"end":{"line":1853},"content_hash":"d6db51fbfe5931fb0d00605685ea2de5cccafa046c6c89f623e78fc68fb20aa2"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"760c3ecf2634766a9223257315a1abad9ab19a93980997c270802bf810a32240","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:11.482674Z","id":"f4869932695aeee77565cbd0f2bd6859a744672ee8ca61df10f9e18002df3623","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Obsolete: content keys are gone on main (content_key, asset_key and clip_key removed from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs; content is served on its artifact's site under the site access check, crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs), and main closed this thread's root ad4d8d8c with resolve 11ae2ec2. This head is an earlier re-anchor of the same record.","supersedes":"e5499b42c4471ec4cde83df826bf879f8203a8877e4a3338eea41dbc5fbdff71","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:11.557781Z","id":"95d101cba0a591810c7ba1a04bf167fdf4b92652666e62a46a325731121c50f2","body":{"detail":"holder_reads takes no hosted flag (its callers, SiteCredentials::check and caller_holder among them, hold only the store), so Holder::Owner is checked by MemberRights::owner(st).allows_at on both kinds of daemon. On a local daemon artifacts.person is NULL for every artifact, so Store::reach is Within and the owner's full rights allow the read, as before. A local home holding an artifact with a person set (one copied from a hosted home) would refuse the owner's site session for it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":407},"end":{"line":409},"content_hash":"38e1d3520b926f2d66e104876ee82f48bb1ac1697749de652311d261a4e1f289"},"suggested_fix":"Pass whether the daemon is hosted to holder_reads and allow Holder::Owner outright on a local one.","summary":"holder_reads holds the owner to MemberRights::owner on a local daemon too, where it allows every artifact only because none there names a person","tags":["hosted","reach","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:11.557830Z","id":"6219096a4179be30c229bd350d56def30d9b4c282c54213c21c2c8cfe467fcc5","body":{"detail":"Subscriber::resolve calls site_caller, whose Holder::Owner is admin whatever the artifact, while resolve_at (the room routes) calls site_caller_at, which on a hosted daemon makes the owner admin only at an artifact the owner made. resolve's one caller, GET /api/events (crates/clax-server/src/routes/events.rs), is not a site API route (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs inner), so no site request reaches it today; a site route added on Subscriber::resolve would give the owner admin documents on a page shared with them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":582},"end":{"line":589},"content_hash":"8391b482fe8de265a3f3efcbde6bf8c9acdd65accd62eb097d807c00b398616d"},"suggested_fix":"Drop the site arm from Subscriber::resolve, or make every site caller go through site_caller_at with the artifact.","summary":"Subscriber::resolve gives a site's owner holder admin at any artifact; only resolve_at holds the owner to the reach","tags":["hosted","reach","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T15:08:26.355227Z","id":"e205171a887c3cee7d25594a566068c5752f9f78023a3c488b0780a946dab7f2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:66b52c08","summary":"Fixed in 66b52c08: holder_reads and SiteCredentials::check take whether the daemon is hosted, and Holder::Owner reads every artifact on a local one (crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs). Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-mcp:integration__1 and //crates/clax-server:integration__1 to __5 pass, among them api_canary::the_owner_by_hand_sees_every_canary and api_drafts's two site tests (a local daemon's owner reading a person's site), which failed before it, and api_site_access's hosted reach tests.","supersedes":"95d101cba0a591810c7ba1a04bf167fdf4b92652666e62a46a325731121c50f2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T15:08:26.434026Z","id":"e68895d3fe9cb500abe78689577223739b977b13e5d4da0fb9227a17f7ad0675","body":{"detail":"SiteCredentials::check runs when Event::Access, Event::SiteAccess or a new version reaches a holder's socket (crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs RoomCheck::ask), before the next message after one, and when the Worker reopens it; each check renews the site session. A socket's own messages renew it too, at most every SITE_SESSION_RENEW_SECS (crates/clax-store/src/site_sessions.rs; RoomCheck::renewal_due and RoomCheck::renew, on the daemon and the Worker), so a socket in use outlives SITE_SESSION_TTL_SECS (test: api_site_access::a_site_room_socket_in_use_outlives_its_sessions_first_hour). A socket that sends nothing for SITE_SESSION_TTL_SECS lets its session expire, and the next such event or wake closes it 4403 revoked, as that test's owner socket shows; its page has to reopen through a new site session. A browser session that expires on its own TTL emits no event either, and closes it the same way. Accepted: the room client (web/bridge/src/caps/room-socket.ts) sends no keep-alive, and a page that sent nothing for an hour loses only its socket, not a right.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":161},"content_hash":"635eb65081d5bf2d6c5f63c1568c52c97ec73e1750ab3d907f01adcf73333335"},"summary":"A site room socket left unused past its site session's TTL closes at the next access change or wake, though its holder still reads","supersedes":"a2bc156c306600423c10a0c7be049efd63e77186662d7dc5e781e5a50fcc1be2","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
