{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T16:31:23.866420Z","id":"e57326dd26a914556db43d94e4f88aee07476048756bd2161fb259e46f0edcc4","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 20a84754 (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:650:674): the same record re-anchored on two lines of history (this branch's rebases and main), differing only in the span it cites.","supersedes":"b0159d89c908a1f2da6e9aa8a64a0e5e0db5d4e236e2be189c66329c9cba0b40","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/grant_auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:14:33.626940Z","id":"f633da6c670ae197b92d6c5f6b27cae3aea2a8a8961380140f1b8515a55b6351","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design §5.3 asks for rate limits per reporter_id and per service grant. crates/clax-http/src/limits.rs holds only body caps, and no request limiter exists to reuse. The only bound is the queue nonce cache: QUEUE_NONCES_PER_KEY (1024 signed requests per key per 240 s window, then 429 limit_reached) and QUEUE_KEYS (16384 keys across every queue). A deployer's backend can mint a fresh reporter key per request, so neither cap bounds one reporter_id or one grant; and one queue's reporters can fill QUEUE_KEYS, refusing every other queue's reporters with 429 until their nonces age out.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":479},"end":{"line":490},"content_hash":"42495ede7d680bd724f40f3ddad60135ac17a9268c644fe7d3295122a7bcbd5d"},"suggested_fix":"Add a per-(queue, reporter_id) and per-service-grant token bucket in clax-http (injected clock), checked in ServiceCaller/ReporterCaller after the token lookup, and give each queue its own share of the key cap.","summary":"A queue's service and reporter routes have no rate limit per reporter_id or per service grant, only a nonce cap per signing key","tags":["security","hosted","queues","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/grant_auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:24:00.334516Z","id":"5e9c8e8be0fba83dcbd795f251bc278324a62c03d16f6343bb3840b14c861f8f","body":{"detail":"head() reads header::HOST as received; the signer (web/sdk/src/sign.ts, crates/clax-core/src/sig.rs) signs the host it sent to. A Kubernetes ingress or other proxy that forwards with its own Host (for example an upstream service name) makes every grant, service and reporter request answer 401 invalid_signature. A deployment must preserve Host (nginx proxy_set_header Host $host; most ingresses do by default), or the daemon must be told its public host. docs/ has no deployment note saying so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":786},"end":{"line":791},"content_hash":"4d0b883080ecbccae4cb839850652c733221076b55d09370ba8747d0a4ccec86"},"summary":"A signed request verifies against the Host header the daemon receives, so a reverse proxy or ingress that rewrites Host breaks every signature","tags":["queues","deploy","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:17:45.840604Z","id":"423720eb55940917aab1c325b17de4c1909873386a19aeb7a68ee80f4988cfcc","body":{"detail":"Identity::quick_caller (and Identity::caller's token branch below it) counts the bearer token as Caller::Owner unless the request names a session (its path or X-Clax-Session) or carries X-Clax-Channel: agent. The hooks and the MCP shim send those (crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs DaemonClient sends X-Clax-Channel: agent), so an agent that has not tampered with its client is always OwnerAgent. An agent that reads <home>/daemon.json itself (0600, but readable by every process of the owner's OS user) and sends the token without them, or runs `CLAX_CHANNEL=owner clax ...` (crates/clax-commands/src/channel.rs), cannot be told from the owner's CLI by the daemon. The decisions only a person at the owner's browser makes need an owner browser session, never the token alone (clax_http::auth::require_owner_browser; crates/clax-server/src/routes/grants.rs require_browser, crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs owner_browser), but such an agent can open a session by driving POST /api/browser-login and GET /login itself. Only OS-level sandboxing of agents (no read of daemon.json) closes this. Open question for the owner: whether to also require a confirmation in the owner's browser for every owner-level write made with the bearer token while an agent session is live.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":288},"end":{"line":297},"content_hash":"0252aa7dc64fe2eb6096e16279c4a8412e0ae74c9db2d597c453b86bddaa04d1"},"summary":"An agent running as the owner's OS user can read daemon.json and send the token unmarked, so it is the Owner; only OS-level sandboxing of agents closes that","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:17:45.840859Z","id":"4ea6511a72b5b63091725e209abc4eedece75dbb90f90a2a3986f3435ce4c02f","body":{"detail":"local_trust::gate admits a request whose clax_viewer cookie names a viewer row. Viewers that GET /api/viewers/me minted for any loopback browser before the login existed keep their cookies, so a request carrying one comments, resolves and sends threads to agents as that viewer (never with owner power). A process of the owner's OS user that reads a browser's cookie jar has them, which is the residue the waiver on crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs (Identity::quick_caller) records. No new such viewer is minted: the gate refuses GET /api/viewers/me with no credential, so the set only shrinks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":393},"end":{"line":402},"content_hash":"e3374226978af713e191cd3fdbbcfb93345660ec26ad6754aa5505c1edffa282"},"suggested_fix":"Forget the cookies of local viewers that are neither the owner nor a person in a later migration, once nothing relies on them.","summary":"A clax_viewer cookie minted before the browser login passes the local gate at a viewer's level","tags":["security","local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:17:45.841005Z","id":"853cca409593eacf9e4b1f20d830319e7dda49ac7cbc268f2473c6b4f31be59d","body":{"detail":"Sessions are revocable in the store and the daemon's cache (OwnerSessions::end, Store::end_owner_session; crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs an_owner_session_survives_a_restart_and_ends_when_revoked), but nothing a person uses calls it: a lost or shared browser profile stays the owner's for 400 days.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"c0bd3164d73296a6925189151cb740a9e2135394812ac3307937fb32611d2ac7"},"suggested_fix":"A `clax logout` (every session, or the browser's own) and a list of sessions in Settings.","summary":"No route or command ends an owner browser session","tags":["local-trust","follow-up","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/discovery_cache.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T01:47:02.020211Z","id":"d7b3182ad26a55cf1b91fcc38f18b58a8d884e712a9db85998cce579cadb5e2e","body":{"detail":"put_clax keeps a positive answer until DiscoveryCache::forget (an instance's name and site_domain rarely change, and re-asking costs every resolution of its URLs a request). A TTL would pick up a renamed instance or a new site_domain without any failure, at the price of a discovery request per origin per TTL.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"a5ed8fe817dcc9d9053d5e5dc147cfb9d9ed711612d6bb0916703b8833a581a3"},"summary":"Keep a Clax instance's discovery answer for a fixed TTL instead of until a call to it fails","tags":["revisit:an instance's name or site_domain changes and the resolver keeps answering the old one because no call to it failed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-30T02:08:15.926083Z","id":"bca1d5ccbefc9e0b1b029ce8eb6219029431ddb3ea41cf4d5f4b572551e06834","body":{"detail":"add the narrower version to the plan","kind":"comment","references":"423720eb55940917aab1c325b17de4c1909873386a19aeb7a68ee80f4988cfcc","summary":"Decided: the narrower version — while an agent session is live, a short list of decisions made with the bare token needs a click in the owner's browser (answering an agent's question, pushing to a remote, connecting a remote or answering a connection request, widening a page's access, approving machines and changing or revoking people); plan Task 8 in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-29-remote-instances.md","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T03:34:46.862935Z","id":"413647e8180910960cb2cf8249ecafcf56012ef90258a704739be4f91ff76c1d","body":{"detail":"require_confirmation (crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs) trusts any owner browser session whose login code was minted while no agent session was live (crates/clax-store/src/browser_login.rs create_login_code), and the in-process app's frame. An agent holding the daemon token can still: (1) drive a browser that already holds such a session (the owner's own, through automation or a browser it launches with the owner's profile) and click Confirm on /inbox?confirm=<id>; (2) mint a login code with POST /api/browser-login before it registers its session (or between sessions, while none is live) and redeem it, getting a session that is not marked minted_while_agent; (3) mint an extension credential with the token (POST /api/extension/credentials, RequireToken; see waiver b5b54c3e on crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs), which browser_of counts as Trusted for the decisions themselves, though not for answering a confirmation. The key cookie (its value is the token) is counted as the token. Accepted: the confirmation raises the cost from one curl call to driving a browser or timing a login before any session registers; only user presence the agent cannot script closes it (see the alternative on this file).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"ab4566484367eae576f9b503a5a4efff0ddb88ec43fd35d335f76bc4bcd7dc77"},"summary":"An agent running as the owner's OS user can still confirm through a browser it drives, or through a session from a login code minted while no agent session was live","tags":["security","residual","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T03:34:46.863161Z","id":"cdd40dc734618a57f3be2d48e88efc3d51201f43db26b27a30ef603883ab7619","body":{"detail":"POST /api/confirmations/<id> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/confirmations.rs answer) accepts a click from an owner browser session; an agent that drives that browser can click it. A WebAuthn assertion with user verification (UV) requires the person's presence, which an agent cannot script. Not now: it needs a passkey registration flow on a local daemon (an RP ID for localhost and every bound address), a fallback for browsers and machines without an authenticator, and the Clax app's WebView, none of which exist yet.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"ab4566484367eae576f9b503a5a4efff0ddb88ec43fd35d335f76bc4bcd7dc77"},"summary":"Confirm with WebAuthn user verification (a passkey or Touch ID) instead of a click in the owner's browser","tags":["security","revisit:a confirmation is seen made by a script or an agent-driven browser","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T03:34:46.863303Z","id":"6af690362c9716213f1791e840c51efaeb13826843c414b2e069e26558122d24","body":{"detail":"browser_of maps an OwnerSession marked key (crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs OwnerSession::key, set for the clax_key_<port> cookie, whose value is the daemon token) to Untrusted, since any token holder can send that cookie. The app that starts a daemon with require_credential and puts the key cookie in its WebView (apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_host.dart) therefore gets 202 confirmation_pending for answering a question, pushing, connecting a remote or opening a site to the world while an agent session is live, and POST /api/confirmations/<id> answers it 403 browser_required. The in-process frame (clax-embed, OwnerSession::browser) is unaffected. Options: give the app's WebView a real owner browser session (a login code redeemed at start, before any agent registers), or accept that the app confirms in a browser.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":132},"end":{"line":154},"content_hash":"700bd08c06e2515f3f1ef72b62f5f9a646f2622c0ce64966e70d717336f5689d"},"summary":"The Clax app's key cookie counts as the token: its WebView cannot answer a confirmation, and its own decisions 1-4 wait while an agent is live","tags":["status:needs-decision","clax-app","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T03:36:15.349849Z","id":"98a7d508d27537958c47f49e7967bdcdf4cd99f040bc4e25cb59590ecb20c008","body":{"detail":"browser_of maps an OwnerSession marked key (crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs OwnerSession::key, set for the clax_key_<port> cookie, whose value is the daemon token) to Untrusted, since any token holder can send that cookie. The app that starts a daemon with require_credential and puts the key cookie in its WebView (apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_host.dart) therefore gets 202 confirmation_pending for answering a question, pushing, connecting a remote or opening a site to the world while an agent session is live, and POST /api/confirmations/<id> answers it 403 browser_required. The in-process frame (clax-embed, OwnerSession::browser) is unaffected. Options: give the app's WebView a real owner browser session (a login code redeemed at start, before any agent registers), or accept that the app confirms in a browser.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":157},"content_hash":"1e2123d4378f7138bfb327d7421b78fcd1120970dd315995b79be1d7c14eb080"},"summary":"The Clax app's key cookie counts as the token: its WebView cannot answer a confirmation, and its own decisions 1-4 wait while an agent is live","supersedes":"6af690362c9716213f1791e840c51efaeb13826843c414b2e069e26558122d24","tags":["status:needs-decision","clax-app","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:10:29.110925Z","id":"7ef82ec2361fe6b49941eb962431453bd16599ff3d95314bdee5a449e46f7312","body":{"detail":"require_confirmation (crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs) trusts an owner browser session whose login code was minted while no agent of the owner's on this machine was live or ended within CONFIRMATION_TTL_SECS (crates/clax-store/src/confirmations.rs LIVE_AGENT, used by create_login_code), the in-process app's frame, and a paired extension. Pairing the extension while an agent is live is itself a confirmed decision (Decision::ExtensionMint on POST /api/extension/credentials). An agent holding the daemon token can still: (1) drive a browser that already holds a trusted session (the owner's own, through automation or a browser launched with the owner's profile) and click Confirm on /inbox?confirm=<id>; (2) mint a login code or an extension credential before it registers its first session, while no agent of the owner's has been live for ten minutes, and keep it. The key cookie (its value is the token) is counted as the token. Accepted: the confirmation raises the cost from one curl call to driving a browser or pairing before any session registers; only user presence the agent cannot script closes it (see the alternative on this file).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"dea843371e180e54044823783a44b9baa36036551bd55a1bea3ac02b728d2738"},"summary":"An agent running as the owner's OS user can still confirm through a browser it drives, or through a session from a login code minted while none of the owner's agents was live","supersedes":"413647e8180910960cb2cf8249ecafcf56012ef90258a704739be4f91ff76c1d","tags":["security","residual","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:10:29.274607Z","id":"9f36af3f52c3b1dcdb111645b8929e247e7806f07c21e4dfb1079ac359d67bec","body":{"detail":"POST /api/confirmations/<id> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/confirmations.rs answer) accepts a click from a trusted owner browser session; an agent that drives that browser can click it. A WebAuthn assertion with user verification (UV) requires the person's presence, which an agent cannot script. Not now: it needs a passkey registration flow on a local daemon (an RP ID for localhost and every bound address), a fallback for browsers and machines without an authenticator, and the Clax app's WebView, none of which exist yet.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"dea843371e180e54044823783a44b9baa36036551bd55a1bea3ac02b728d2738"},"summary":"Confirm with WebAuthn user verification (a passkey or Touch ID) instead of a click in the owner's browser","supersedes":"cdd40dc734618a57f3be2d48e88efc3d51201f43db26b27a30ef603883ab7619","tags":["security","revisit:a confirmation is seen made by a script or an agent-driven browser","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:10:29.455569Z","id":"b1852380122a1adf23028321f09891b7a9bd89c31feb062a2a93118f3e8803b9","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Controller's ruling: the app confirms through its in-process embed path (clax_embed_call), which no agent can reach. That path exists already: the Clax app's shell calls are relayed by crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs (owner-browser frames) marked OwnerSession::browser(), which browser_of counts as Trusted, and the current app holds no key cookie (apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_host.dart clears the old daemon's clax_key_<port> cookies). Evidence: crates/clax-embed/tests/embed.rs the_apps_shell_confirms_a_held_decision_in_process passes (bazelisk test //crates/clax-embed:embed): the app's own code (an owner frame, the token) opening a site to the world while an agent is live answers 202, an owner frame's POST /api/confirmations/<id> is 403 browser_required, and an owner-browser frame's is 200, after which the call goes ahead. The key cookie itself stays counted as the token.","supersedes":"98a7d508d27537958c47f49e7967bdcdf4cd99f040bc4e25cb59590ecb20c008","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:30:47.960958Z","id":"4340ad06eea34153d6ab8ea83c8fd2f29669c4bcce3b57962de213c709002128","body":{"detail":"By default require_confirmation (crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs) lets any owner browser session decide and answer a confirmation. An agent holding the daemon token can mint a login code (POST /api/browser-login), redeem it, and so decide or confirm as the owner's browser; it can also drive a browser that already holds a session, or pair the extension before it registers its first session (pairing while an agent is live is itself confirmed, Decision::ExtensionMint). The bare token and the key cookie (its value is the token) still wait. The residual applies only while passkeys are not required: with a passkey registered and required (crates/clax-store/src/passkeys.rs, crates/clax-server/src/routes/passkeys.rs), every browser session's and the extension's listed decisions wait for a confirmation, and approving one takes a WebAuthn assertion with user verification over a challenge bound to that confirmation, which an agent cannot script. Left even then: the first passkey's registration is confirmed by any owner browser session (an agent could register its own software passkey before the owner does), and the in-process app's frame is exempt (no agent reaches it).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"f7d7d5cc921ed53d81ca2cf9b73d4d10d9787e6f525bf4fa0d73905d0fb10eb4"},"summary":"While passkeys are not required, an agent running as the owner's OS user can still confirm through a browser session it opens or drives","supersedes":"7ef82ec2361fe6b49941eb962431453bd16599ff3d95314bdee5a449e46f7312","tags":["security","residual","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:30:48.108561Z","id":"8eba9d303a482ac3334d40d68f4789f0908da5ec7ae97d208ab7e7f22fdc51ef","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Taken, as the owner's opt-in: Touch ID or another passkey (WebAuthn with user verification) may be required to confirm, offered on the first confirmation card and in Settings. Verification is crates/clax-core/src/webauthn.rs (ES256 and EdDSA on ring, no attestation); routes crates/clax-server/src/routes/passkeys.rs. Evidence: crates/clax-server/tests/api_confirmations.rs with_passkeys_required_confirming_takes_a_valid_assertion, with_passkeys_required_a_browser_sessions_decisions_ask, registering_a_passkey_while_an_agent_is_live_is_confirmed and turning_passkeys_off_takes_an_assertion pass (bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__*), and crates/clax-core/src/webauthn.rs's unit tests (//crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test).","supersedes":"9f36af3f52c3b1dcdb111645b8929e247e7806f07c21e4dfb1079ac359d67bec","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:30:48.268992Z","id":"ce874df931567178b1a72229d68a6265eeb3a1e2295b744036e52146a0a844a0","body":{"detail":"passkey_rp answers None unless the daemon's browser address (AppState::browser_base) is http://localhost or a .localhost host: WebAuthn needs a secure context, and an IP literal is no valid RP ID. There POST /api/passkeys/challenge answers 403 passkey_unavailable, no passkey can be registered, the Settings switch (web/shell/src/q/PasskeySettings.svelte) is disabled and says why, and the waiver on this file's residual holds in full. A passkey registered at localhost is not asked for by a request that arrives at the LAN address either: the requirement is the store's (passkeys_required), so a browser at the LAN address is refused 403 passkey_required or passkey_refused (its origin is not the RP's) rather than let through.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":434},"end":{"line":445},"content_hash":"349ac496d8105a7963b31a27a6e6adfecf146de90b06455385bc64cbb1de850e"},"summary":"On a daemon whose browser address is a LAN IP (no secure context, no valid RP ID), passkeys cannot be used and confirming stays by any owner browser session","tags":["security","passkeys","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:31:12.637557Z","id":"35cc30f344d9a141b696988ce1d5cba9b1fbd44381c5593bf837a24d1204d332","body":{"detail":"Let users configure Touch ID / passkey if they prefer on first use / in configuration","kind":"comment","references":"4340ad06eea34153d6ab8ea83c8fd2f29669c4bcce3b57962de213c709002128","summary":"Decided: confirmation by any owner browser session by default; Touch ID / passkey user verification opt-in on first use or in Settings","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:53:02.807188Z","id":"d224b3bc5bf9c2e2837872b86fe72f4b9395f876fd17515eaeff7e5d28e20d6e","body":{"detail":"By default require_confirmation (crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs) lets any owner browser session decide and answer a confirmation. An agent holding the daemon token can mint a login code (POST /api/browser-login), redeem it, and so decide or confirm as the owner's browser; it can also drive a browser that already holds a session, or pair the extension before it registers its first session (pairing while an agent is live is itself confirmed, Decision::ExtensionMint). The bare token and the key cookie (its value is the token) still wait. With a passkey registered and required (crates/clax-store/src/passkeys.rs, crates/clax-server/src/routes/passkeys.rs), every browser session's and the extension's listed decisions wait for a confirmation, and approving one takes a WebAuthn assertion with user verification over a challenge bound to that confirmation, which an agent cannot script. Accepted takeover (the agent runs as the owner's OS user): before the owner registers a passkey, an agent-opened session can register its own (confirmed by any owner browser session, the agent's own included) and require passkeys; then only the agent's key confirms, turns the requirement off or removes passkeys, and the owner is locked out. The same lockout holds when passkeys were required at localhost and the daemon is later served at a LAN address, where no passkey works. Visibility: every passkey shows its creation time, the browser that added it and the owner's agents live then (GET /api/passkeys added_by; the first-use offer, a confirmation that requires a passkey, Settings). Recovery: with the daemon stopped, `clax passkeys reset` (crates/clax-commands/src/commands/passkeys.rs, docs/usage.md) removes every passkey and turns the requirement off, printing what it removed; an agent running as the owner could run it too, after stopping the daemon. The in-process app's frame is exempt from passkeys (no agent reaches it).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"f7d7d5cc921ed53d81ca2cf9b73d4d10d9787e6f525bf4fa0d73905d0fb10eb4"},"summary":"While passkeys are not required, an agent running as the owner's OS user can still confirm through a browser session it opens or drives; before the owner adds one, it can add its own and lock the owner out until `clax passkeys reset`","supersedes":"4340ad06eea34153d6ab8ea83c8fd2f29669c4bcce3b57962de213c709002128","tags":["security","residual","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:53:03.439194Z","id":"a546bbf089884ab1aaac26c39aade876964c2199cdd08256bc86256bfb16e210","body":{"detail":"passkey_rp answers None unless the daemon's browser address (AppState::browser_base) is http://localhost or a .localhost host: WebAuthn needs a secure context, and an IP literal is no valid RP ID. There POST /api/passkeys/challenge answers 403 passkey_unavailable, no passkey can be registered, the Settings switch (web/shell/src/q/PasskeySettings.svelte) is disabled and says why, and the waiver on this file's residual holds in full. Passkeys required at localhost stay required (passkeys_required reads the store alone), so a browser at the LAN address is refused 403 passkey_required or passkey_refused (its origin is not the RP's) rather than let through, and no confirmation can be approved there. Recovery: stop the daemon and run `clax passkeys reset` (docs/usage.md), which removes every passkey and turns the requirement off.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":440},"end":{"line":451},"content_hash":"349ac496d8105a7963b31a27a6e6adfecf146de90b06455385bc64cbb1de850e"},"summary":"On a daemon whose browser address is a LAN IP (no secure context, no valid RP ID), passkeys cannot be used: with none required, confirming stays by any owner browser session; with passkeys required at localhost before, nothing confirms until `clax passkeys reset`","supersedes":"ce874df931567178b1a72229d68a6265eeb3a1e2295b744036e52146a0a844a0","tags":["security","passkeys","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/state.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T06:25:57.782416Z","id":"8f6584ddc429e01194a3da9aad0d0ebed69c6ab83f9c10043477870222b5c126","body":{"detail":"sessions_ended (and the daemon's reaper in crates/clax-server/src/core.rs) call linked.kick(None) so a followed artifact's session there ends with its local session. Each kick runs a cycle per remote with a link (a read of each link's threads changed since its cursor); kicking only the remotes whose followed mirrors the ended sessions watched needs their watches read before the end.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":323},"content_hash":"d608acde301ba978898ba60a5de2ccea12b5dca8b3c971a17cb52ee72250f6b8"},"summary":"Every session end wakes every remote's linked-threads cycle","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:41:02.598922Z","id":"d5b12f22713f47c228fd87b9f1cde069b339357dc5af3661821d598134183c35","body":{"detail":"Failure: the owner opens a link, redirect or page that navigates the browser to http://localhost:<other port>/ (or the daemon's LAN address on another port). The browser sends clax_owner_<daemon port>=cxb_... there, since cookies ignore ports. Whoever listens on that port (another OS user, a container port-mapped to loopback, an agent sandboxed without file access but with loopback networking, a dev server that logs headers) replays it: curl -H 'Host: localhost:7480' -H 'Cookie: clax_owner_7480=cxb_...' http://127.0.0.1:7480/api/token answers the daemon token. The replay passes session_counts (crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs:247): a loopback peer with a local Host, no Origin, no Sec-Fetch-Site.\n\nAccepted for now, with a way out: DELETE /api/browser-login and `clax logout` end every owner browser session (crates/clax-server/src/routes/login.rs, end_all), and every daemon start ends them, since it makes a new token (crates/clax-server/src/core.rs, Core::start). docs/contract.md (\"The owner and other viewers\") states the residual. Copies replayed from another machine stay useless (from_this_machine).\n\nOptions for the owner:\n(A) Accept the residual as it stands: ending sessions (logout, restart) is the remedy.\n(B) Recommended: a port-scoped second factor. /login redirects through a page that writes half of the session secret into localStorage (per origin, port included); /api/token and owner writes require it as a header, bound to the session's hash, so the cookie alone confers only page loads. The realtime transport (EventSource on /api/events, the room WebSocket) sends no custom header and needs the proof another way, for example a short-lived ticket minted with the header.\n(C) A short session lifetime (hours, not OWNER_SESSION_TTL_SECS's 400 days) with silent renewal while the shell is open, so a captured cookie lapses soon.\n\nNote: since every daemon start now ends every session, a browser of the owner's needs `clax open` again after each restart (the openers mint a login code for it).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":278},"end":{"line":299},"content_hash":"c1c3fdee903be73cf04167b43d266c7404d057ac665d63be192b06b648ad0473"},"summary":"The owner cookie is host-only but not port-scoped: a server on another port of the daemon's host that the browser is navigated to receives it and can replay it as the owner","tags":["security","local-trust","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:41:02.599471Z","id":"dc8971df9bdfc4eaa218859688af07f676ad22f611fa8ac07b6af10c0bb068f7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"853cca409593eacf9e4b1f20d830319e7dda49ac7cbc268f2473c6b4f31be59d","summary":"Sessions can now be ended: DELETE /api/browser-login and `clax logout` end every one (OwnerSessions::end_all), and every daemon start ends them with its new token. The residual that motivates ending them (the cookie reaches other ports of the host) is the waiver on crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs:278:299.","tags":["local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:41:25.561845Z","id":"5ad0fd4238d011ac924a0317e1e42ab1f719eaaffe93bfabb8bd2340247a3031","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:abfe8771e","summary":"Fixed in abfe8771e: DELETE /api/browser-login (`clax logout`) ends every owner browser session, and Core::start ends them with each new token. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server/... passes api_local_trust::the_owner_ends_every_browser_session_at_once and core_start::a_new_daemon_token_ends_every_owner_browser_session; //crates/clax-cli/... passes cli::open_hands_the_browser_a_login_link_and_prints_none, which runs `clax logout --json` and sees the cookie answer 401 after.","supersedes":"853cca409593eacf9e4b1f20d830319e7dda49ac7cbc268f2473c6b4f31be59d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:12.267029Z","id":"e8cd6cedaca6afca4ddb614bf64b163ca8c70a967c21c73737f515338c654fa9","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:503-503, record fced511a.\n\napi_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":673},"end":{"line":673},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"35b8b1427337b5bdcf776f42a01baaecd171c03f6f11364bbc64c202a99592fa","tags":["people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:12.358249Z","id":"590d30bf9d0725a42ef49265d4394efc2c7c212df517e5e848e3758250b848f7","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:998-998, record 3c0ad45d.\n\nEvery handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:1166:1166 to crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:1284:1284: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1394},"end":{"line":1394},"content_hash":"70159c01f5d2722d2fc4945c93216b297a9e269ea1785d2c1539aabdc32321d7"},"summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"b957fff428e8d307c88c895c51614fd47a53019a70c48fb96a14273182f52221","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:12.453912Z","id":"a299b6446e4b4123af50c5dfbb64656a531f1d07740643b9fe16e5a754e34341","body":{"detail":"verify_bearer hands a person-device grant a PersonDevice whose who is the person's member session (Store::person_device_viewer), and crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs browser_or_device takes it as that session: may_share and session_reads read the person's rights, never the grant's narrowing. Narrowing applies to a grant's sessions (Store::grant_caller); the Clax app's token opens none on these routes. A person who narrows the app's token on People still lets it share every artifact they made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2266},"end":{"line":2287},"content_hash":"ac6260549d2bff9f04aa3a9c74651b357e21dee778ee91f1b320200da366acc8"},"suggested_fix":"Intersect with Store::grant_caller(gid, None)'s rights in person_device_viewer's caller, or hide Narrow for kind device on People.","summary":"A person's device acts on sharing with its person's full rights: narrowing its grant (PUT /api/people/me/grants/<gid>/narrow) does not limit it","supersedes":"f2415df240c8904293bf1bbb53ee8d6de293bbe39bdcb552c6fd38d3d9eaba25","tags":["security","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:12.546296Z","id":"5edac47cf5a29da09356933c121939e81d4281197dd4738669260a269d8a35cb","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs:153-171, record 36bf936e.\n\nis_grant_request includes Bearer cxa_…, and verify_layer admits it wherever a route's need! admits grants, so a script holding an agent token can call the API directly with the same rights its MCP tools have. The prototype (hosted/src/mcp/server.ts) took the token only at /mcp. The rights are identical either way; restricting it to in-process requests from the adapter would need a marker the loopback sets.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":155},"end":{"line":173},"content_hash":"e6eb9b5cd97f310ac94ca698005b960357df7ef98121b5cc7bb8c8f5000f777c"},"summary":"An agent token is an agent credential on every route a grant may reach, not only through the MCP adapter","supersedes":"4af60633c0e68b7e88e490427b950bd7b32cf5497852ab10d650b2e0734db5aa","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:12.638172Z","id":"f8fee366b7824008e493c0ab43a1374fda09c13eefd3e5781ec09be777dd63e3","body":{"detail":"axum 0.8.9 src/serve/listener.rs:30-37 loops 'match Self::accept(self).await { Ok(tup) => return tup, Err(e) => handle_accept_error(e).await }'. handle_accept_error (:140-158) returns at once when is_connection_error (:160-167: ConnectionRefused, ConnectionAborted, ConnectionReset), else logs 'error!(\"accept error: {e}\")' and runs 'tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_secs(1)).await'. So a listener the OS has reclaimed (iOS may close a suspended app's sockets) costs one error log line a second and never ends serve: the daemon keeps running on a dead socket until its host notices (a failing /healthz) and stops and restarts it. Checked against the axum 0.8.9 source crate_universe fetched (Cargo.lock pins axum 0.8.9).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":452},"content_hash":"8ed331101280a14d1d68691a00f18a00232b6e51e8a7fc0d11160a1249d21299"},"summary":"TunedListener::accept never returns an accept error: axum 0.8.9's Listener for TcpListener retries every one, at once for a per-connection error and after a 1 s sleep for any other","supersedes":"a901b7b806a523eb647a2a1e62610efbb8b1eb878cdcc583f9bb97589a99235a","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:12.730307Z","id":"434e02d66cb4978ff8d752e5034beed3e3883108ecc93e6723379ac5464dd621","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:197-200, record ed323928.\n\nLimits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":261},"end":{"line":264},"content_hash":"e773e1438242b272aff7abb4426e25b6868af8c1d503cc1f0ab28083fc52603f"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"9e59786e305b782dbf52fbe99a1e02f90cc30313ce4eb8ffe055a5d1fe2b0dad","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:12.821096Z","id":"50c69b4671affa60f570790e15dbabe5047cbdb9cea6623172b05ae1c34ac6cb","body":{"detail":"owners_people_view removes from each access object the locations naming artifacts out of the owner's reach and counts them in hidden_locations (tested by api_hosted::the_owners_people_names_no_page_of_another_person). PUT /api/people/<pid>/rights (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs set_rights) replaces a person's rights with the value sent, and the shell (web/shell/src/people) builds that value from what People showed, so the owner re-saving a person's rights drops the hidden locations. Those include artifact IDs of the person's own pages, which are within the person's reach and do grant there (a location naming another person's artifact has no effect on hosted). Raises are per granter and narrowings are the person's own, so only a person's rights round-trip this way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":955},"end":{"line":998},"content_hash":"41294579380e6815f5488408bfbf51e56ec211a988309954a468461835e3bf45"},"suggested_fix":"On hosted, have set_rights keep the stored locations out of the owner's reach when it replaces a person's rights (the owner cannot see them, so cannot mean to drop them), or refuse a value that would drop them.","summary":"A rights value People shows the owner on hosted leaves out hidden locations, so an edit built from it drops them","supersedes":"62e7dd55e7885636aebcd2c52588a6d1ef567b4efb987797f3426fd9093491e1","tags":["hosted","people","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:12.909194Z","id":"59b919d504f1cb9e6179ef742ee666740cd1ff18ecd1fe703558a8916b74901b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:933-937, record a625cb63.\n\nmember_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:930:934 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1263:1267: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1154},"end":{"line":1158},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"bdea98c5e26a0104439c08c862150647ce3289ddcb0236cca175cf77cfb73cfb","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:12.999640Z","id":"cbbfaaa726f64f585f4e15e60148e7d93055a3307264d416e30d2e9393772c88","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1181-1183, record 5d1ab740.\n\nThe prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1178:1180 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1499:1501: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1415},"end":{"line":1417},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"9ddc9cd4c117c62ef3ce99e56f68a6a80de8ee159178ef8d473b9bce992beb50","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:13.088967Z","id":"19a33f5fdfb5942f9743f104e16577a04b57fae1760a96fe8e3f10a9b2783140","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:1607-1615, record 5be58509.\n\nPUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1604:1612 to crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1970:1978: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1914},"end":{"line":1922},"content_hash":"d6db51fbfe5931fb0d00605685ea2de5cccafa046c6c89f623e78fc68fb20aa2"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"a479d008261feb72aa0030afe8b0fd4dc7117f2008c5617d3b11588cf815c7cf","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:13.178786Z","id":"f4491c72e2d4a6683e9cabf3e290a063627574e3250959ca23b5beb80d92a3da","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:496-503, record f3b6a110.\n\nIdentity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":709},"end":{"line":716},"content_hash":"e518245782ac10f00f2b65f20d7c675055af73af8c7fb3c52ec0df3ab6eb723b"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"c77c0394c086d807772f6441102c3ff94e064baf6b44658b4202fd6529dfe544","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:23.771031Z","id":"8ac5cb2dc6232e3540bd4128abba4b8afd814f6d0ea7ae3f1414c9716373068a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5aa5c8a7894e8bb753fffdf37984e28d7015653ad0984725f4117a8cb7f0b5f0","summary":"Drifted and not re-anchored: the lines this record hashed (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:114:160 at 2bbefe713, origin/main) were changed by branch remote-instances; its longest line, `\"this daemon serves this machine alone, and the machines and browsers of people connected to it\",`, is now at line 153, but the lines around it changed. Whether the record still applies, and where, is for its author or the owner to judge.","tags":["drift","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T09:05:06.377252Z","id":"c613f6a52ee58280df60901ea335246297ca835471c75a7ed4ad1d88288c10b1","body":{"detail":"Failure: the owner opens a link, redirect or page that navigates the browser to http://localhost:<other port>/ (or the daemon's LAN address on another port). The browser sends clax_owner_<daemon port>=cxb_... there, since cookies ignore ports. Whoever listens on that port (another OS user, a container port-mapped to loopback, an agent sandboxed without file access but with loopback networking, a dev server that logs headers) replays it: curl -H 'Host: localhost:7480' -H 'Cookie: clax_owner_7480=cxb_...' http://127.0.0.1:7480/api/token answers the daemon token. The replay passes session_counts (crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs:247): a loopback peer with a local Host, no Origin, no Sec-Fetch-Site.\n\nAccepted for now, with a way out: DELETE /api/browser-login and `clax logout` end every owner browser session (crates/clax-server/src/routes/login.rs, end_all). Sessions survive daemon restarts and the new token each start makes; no other path rotates the token. docs/contract.md (\"The owner and other viewers\") states the residual. Copies replayed from another machine stay useless (from_this_machine).\n\nOptions for the owner:\n(A) Accept the residual as it stands: ending sessions (logout, restart) is the remedy.\n(B) Recommended: a port-scoped second factor. /login redirects through a page that writes half of the session secret into localStorage (per origin, port included); /api/token and owner writes require it as a header, bound to the session's hash, so the cookie alone confers only page loads. The realtime transport (EventSource on /api/events, the room WebSocket) sends no custom header and needs the proof another way, for example a short-lived ticket minted with the header.\n(C) A short session lifetime (hours, not OWNER_SESSION_TTL_SECS's 400 days) with silent renewal while the shell is open, so a captured cookie lapses soon.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":278},"end":{"line":299},"content_hash":"c1c3fdee903be73cf04167b43d266c7404d057ac665d63be192b06b648ad0473"},"summary":"The owner cookie is host-only but not port-scoped: a server on another port of the daemon's host that the browser is navigated to receives it and can replay it as the owner","supersedes":"d5b12f22713f47c228fd87b9f1cde069b339357dc5af3661821d598134183c35","tags":["security","local-trust","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T09:05:06.470903Z","id":"9af2f8cc0f81fcc588cd66e4500a6476876440f91f7ea545e4946588a11301fa","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5ad0fd4238d011ac924a0317e1e42ab1f719eaaffe93bfabb8bd2340247a3031","summary":"Correction to this close and to reply dc8971df: a daemon start no longer ends the sessions (reverted in a0ad033e8, since every start makes a new token and it logged every browser out on each restart). Sessions survive restarts; DELETE /api/browser-login and `clax logout` alone end them, which is what closed 853cca40. core_start::an_owner_browser_session_survives_a_new_daemon_token pins it.","tags":["local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T09:51:33.692232Z","id":"d453e0dfcd722f46d65a7512fd7763e2c099c55a3b84aab550a54b72a87156cb","body":{"detail":"open (98-107) and end_all (129-136) each write the store and then the in-memory map, with no lock held across both, and store calls run on a pool. Interleaved, a session can be live in the store but missing from memory (dead now, back after the next restart), or ended in the store but live in memory (working until the restart). Fix: take the map's write lock before the store call in both, or rebuild the map from live_owner_sessions() after the UPDATE.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"9cc65299f5c85c42040b0ba5ee6b9140e8d9d41239cab3e14fdcd99e58655d2c"},"summary":"A login redeemed while clax logout runs can leave the store and the in-memory session map disagreeing","tags":["review","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T09:51:33.692879Z","id":"1ac4941fc2a9a30f061431bc1296aa968ac81c568dfd65fb8d155af1281ef3fa","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c613f6a52ee58280df60901ea335246297ca835471c75a7ed4ad1d88288c10b1","summary":"Option (A)'s '(logout, restart)' is stale: since a0ad033e8 a restart keeps owner browser sessions, and only clax logout (DELETE /api/browser-login) ends them.","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T22:13:04.344695Z","id":"a781ef76ef93fef46a2981dda56e0f0857d32387ad3097dce15aa2f87c9e309a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5ad0fd4238d011ac924a0317e1e42ab1f719eaaffe93bfabb8bd2340247a3031","summary":"Commit abfe8771e cited by this close was re-signed as 48e03388f (same tree, author and message).","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/state.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:24:44.603648Z","id":"a3e9d943754bcd2b930dce2209d1f9aa00fa0ec0b6a6048622c8b6db8216e5cd","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8f6584ddc429e01194a3da9aad0d0ebed69c6ab83f9c10043477870222b5c126","summary":"Still as recorded: crates/clax-http/src/state.rs:339 and crates/clax-server/src/core.rs:427 call linked.kick(None). A cost, not a failure: each kick is one cheap read per linked remote. Narrowing it needs the ended sessions' followed watches read before the end, as the record says.","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:36:18.266966Z","id":"2bc67359a84d5ae115e73e07ffa1e627c44595675ac6bacaf7710715895529c2","body":{"detail":"viewer_me (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs) makes a guest from PUT /api/viewers/me {display_name} alone, and the shell sends only that (web/shell/src/threads.ts, the guest naming fetch). Options: (A) the shell sends artifact_id and the route requires it to be shared by link for commenting, refusing 403 not_permitted otherwise (a shell and route change together); (B) keep it: a guest without a shared page can do nothing (guest_may refuses every action) and Attempt::Guest bounds the rows to five per client then one per two minutes. Recommendation: A, done with the shell change in one commit, so no deployed shell sends a request the route refuses.","kind":"comment","references":"19a33f5fdfb5942f9743f104e16577a04b57fae1760a96fe8e3f10a9b2783140","summary":"Needs a decision: refusing a guest without a page needs the shell to name the page","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:36:18.267500Z","id":"eadbc050aebd803f678b803a1cadc0e27db2fd1125e196a197e2526a30af50b1","body":{"detail":"As reply 4bf3d2bc says, lists, counts, items, events and attention are filtered by reach on hosted. Marking read an item one cannot see changes only the caller's own read marks, and its ID is not listed to them. Not changed here; the owner may close this or keep it for the mark route.","kind":"comment","references":"59b919d504f1cb9e6179ef742ee666740cd1ff18ecd1fe703558a8916b74901b","summary":"What is left is minor: POST /api/inbox/read {ids} marks an item by its ID without a reach check","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:36:19.456709Z","id":"dcff8e122b054abfeb7339b1d9b3dcebc06849fd27ae9739bc67e9c53776f00f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f98b779d2","summary":"Fixed: on hosted, set_rights adds each stored location People hides back to the new value (keep_hidden_locations, by type, actions and level, else an object of its own). Test api_hosted::saving_a_persons_rights_as_people_shows_them_keeps_the_hidden_locations passes (//crates/clax-server:integration__4) and failed before the fix","supersedes":"50c69b4671affa60f570790e15dbabe5047cbdb9cea6623172b05ae1c34ac6cb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:31:03.082812Z","id":"3277d428c21e46de74539d3f85226e76948ee54ca3785b7207d3859ef3eeff59","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs: OwnerSessions keeps each session's proof hash (owner_browser_sessions.proof_sha256, migration 60), live_session marks a request OwnerSession only when X-Clax-Owner-Proof (or ?owner_proof= on GET /api/events, /api/stream and the room and live sockets, takes_proof_param) proves the cookie's session, else UnprovenSession, which gate admits for a page load alone; crates/clax-server/src/shell/mod.rs artifact_page serves such a load bare. GET /login answers login_page, which stores the proof and goes on to next. The shell sends the proof on every request to its origin (web/shell/src/owner-proof.ts), hands it to the stream worker in each hello (web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts) and puts it in socket addresses. Sessions survive restarts with their proof (crates/clax-server/tests/core_start.rs an_owner_browser_session_survives_a_new_daemon_token). Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server/... passes api_local_trust::an_owner_cookie_replayed_without_its_proof_is_no_credential (the Failure line's replay: GET /api/token with the cookie and the daemon's Host and no proof answers 401 no_credential; with live_session counting the cookie alone, as the code did before 5ecbdf9bc, it fails: /api/token left (200, \"\") right (401, \"no_credential\")) and shell_boot::an_owner_cookie_without_its_proof_gets_the_bare_entry; //crates/clax-http:clax_http_lib_test passes local_trust::tests::a_cookie_without_its_proof_is_unproven and the_proof_rides_the_query_on_the_realtime_routes_alone.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5ecbdf9bc","summary":"Fixed with option (B): an owner browser session is a cookie and a proof the login's page writes into the origin's localStorage; the cookie alone is no credential but for a bare page load","supersedes":"c613f6a52ee58280df60901ea335246297ca835471c75a7ed4ad1d88288c10b1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:31:03.203439Z","id":"c6bc2572782588935474f36fa52efbffbac8d5d5cb814e0fb51bd6e7ab72b6ba","body":{"detail":"OwnerSessions::open, end and end_all (crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs:155-197) now hold one mutex (OwnerSessions::writes) across the store's change and the map's, so a login and clax logout cannot interleave between the two; checking (is_live, proves) reads the map alone. The regression test local_trust::tests::a_login_racing_a_logout_leaves_the_store_and_the_map_agreeing (200 rounds of a concurrent open and end_all, comparing live_owner_sessions with the map after each) passes, but it also passed with the lock removed: the window between a store write and the map update is narrower than thread scheduling reaches. The evidence is the structure, not the test, so this is left for the owner to close.","kind":"comment","references":"d453e0dfcd722f46d65a7512fd7763e2c099c55a3b84aab550a54b72a87156cb","summary":"Fixed in 5ecbdf9bc as suggested, without RED evidence; proposing close to the owner","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:31:03.445652Z","id":"417cb3b18c8bca66cd67e509e8e04cc6c177961f32df2ff12a46ee4d54d5bdcb","body":{"detail":"local_trust::gate (crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs, the clax_viewer branch at the end of gate) admits any cookie naming a viewer row. Like the owner cookie before 5ecbdf9bc, clax_viewer is host-only, SameSite=Lax, Path=/, so a server on another port of the daemon's host receives a legacy local viewer's cookie from the owner's browser and can replay it from this machine: comments, resolves and sends to agents at that viewer's level. The set only shrinks (each browser's cookie is claimed and cleared at its next GET /login, Store::claim_for_owner), and a process of the owner's OS user has the token anyway.\n\nOptions:\n(A) Recommended: the gate admits a clax_viewer cookie only for a live connected person's viewer (viewers.person, not revoked); legacy local viewers' cookies are read only at GET /login (open to anyone), where the claim keeps working. Cost: the test helpers that stand for an anonymous local browser with such a viewer (crates/clax-testkit TestServer::viewer and local_browser, about 300 call sites in crates/*/tests; web/e2e/fixtures.ts localBrowser and asLocalViewer; POST /api/_test/viewers) move to connected persons or the owner.\n(B) A later migration forgets those viewers' cookies (DELETE FROM viewer_cookies for viewers minted_local, not the owner, not a person): simple, but a browser whose cookie is forgotten loses its claim, so its history stays under a viewer the owner never merges.\n(C) Keep the residue until the claims are done.","kind":"comment","references":"4ea6511a72b5b63091725e209abc4eedece75dbb90f90a2a3986f3435ce4c02f","summary":"Confirmed, and wider than the record says: the clax_viewer cookie is not port-scoped either; fixing it needs a call on the login claim and the test helpers","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:31:03.446171Z","id":"f090ac7c1a7c975ec9e1418507cb2b67597de9504865b7b24ab73dbadf514033","body":{"detail":"Identity::audit_actor (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs) returns Actor::Agent with no session and the channel the request names (none for mcp or no channel) when the token names any session, by X-Clax-Session or the session argument, that is not a known one of the token's, as Identity::caller counts it OwnerAgent. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server/... passes api_toolpath::the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent with the new cases (X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 and not-a-ulid, with and without x-clax-via hook); ctx_session_header_is_agent_with_harness_ids and ctx_bad_headers_are_invalid_not_errors, which asserted the owner for such a request against docs/contract.md (a token request that names a session is the owner's agent), are updated in e79ddcd0c and pass; before 645e573f2 the new cases fail with left {\"type\": \"owner\"} right {\"type\": \"agent\", \"session_id\": null}.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:645e573f2","summary":"Fixed: the token naming a session that is not known, without the agent marker, is recorded as the sessionless agent","supersedes":"f4491c72e2d4a6683e9cabf3e290a063627574e3250959ca23b5beb80d92a3da","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/confirm.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:31:03.814414Z","id":"4e6ec435d8ef570714b8a3ce34822411908238023a69e44c2b5cef1d4a419458","body":{"detail":"An owner browser session is now a cookie and a proof (crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs), but GET /login hands both to whoever redeems the code: the proof is in the login page's body (local_trust::login_page). An agent holding the token that drives POST /api/browser-login and GET /login itself reads it as a browser's script does, so it still opens a session that decides and confirms as the owner's browser. The proof closes replay of a captured cookie from another port, not this residual; passkeys required remain what closes it.","kind":"comment","references":"d224b3bc5bf9c2e2837872b86fe72f4b9395f876fd17515eaeff7e5d28e20d6e","summary":"Unchanged by the session proof of 5ecbdf9bc","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:31:03.814823Z","id":"d70140f44a8c6a7c8fd23b024e337d6c276dffd1fcd933357b9367c0a801c047","body":{"detail":"The owner browser session now needs its proof beside its cookie (crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs), but an agent that reads daemon.json and drives POST /api/browser-login and GET /login itself gets the proof from the login page's body (local_trust::login_page) as the browser's script does, so it still opens a session and makes the decisions that need an owner browser. Only OS-level sandboxing of agents (no read of daemon.json) closes this, as the record says.","kind":"comment","references":"423720eb55940917aab1c325b17de4c1909873386a19aeb7a68ee80f4988cfcc","summary":"Unchanged by the session proof of 5ecbdf9bc","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:31:03.815053Z","id":"d5f531e55856b76272ca87f11672559f39a091e0b126d17dbf518ca31984896b","body":{"detail":"request_holder on a local daemon is the owner only for Identity::is_owner, which since 5ecbdf9bc needs the owner browser session's proof beside its cookie. A top-level visit to <id>.localhost (an address opened in a new tab or pasted) reaches GET /site-signin as a navigation, which carries the cookie alone, so crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_signin.rs page finds no holder and sends the browser to /a/<id>, where the shell frames the site with a code it asks for with the proof (POST /api/artifacts/<id>/site-code). Before, the cookie alone signed the visit in on the site itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":761},"end":{"line":764},"content_hash":"0b7a78dd3647261ed98d17eecd4f562810844a3f936417004f58277c7a661636"},"suggested_fix":"If direct site visits should keep working, have /site-signin answer a small page whose script asks POST /api/artifacts/<id>/site-code with the proof from localStorage and goes on to the code's address.","summary":"Opening an artifact's site address directly no longer signs the owner's browser in there; it lands on the artifact's shell page","tags":["local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:43:50.778626Z","id":"090b24064b787c9ccf07c0053c676c0d703e0c58669b256d9aa7610bcddacbb6","body":{"detail":"local_trust::gate admits a request whose clax_viewer cookie names a viewer row. Viewers that GET /api/viewers/me minted for any loopback browser before the login existed keep their cookies, so a request carrying one comments, resolves and sends threads to agents as that viewer (never with owner power). A process of the owner's OS user that reads a browser's cookie jar has them, which is the residue the waiver on crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs (Identity::quick_caller) records. No new such viewer is minted: the gate refuses GET /api/viewers/me with no credential, so the set only shrinks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":887},"end":{"line":896},"content_hash":"e3374226978af713e191cd3fdbbcfb93345660ec26ad6754aa5505c1edffa282"},"suggested_fix":"Forget the cookies of local viewers that are neither the owner nor a person in a later migration, once nothing relies on them.","summary":"A clax_viewer cookie minted before the browser login passes the local gate at a viewer's level","supersedes":"4ea6511a72b5b63091725e209abc4eedece75dbb90f90a2a3986f3435ce4c02f","tags":["security","local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:43:50.876967Z","id":"dfbaf0bbe44f599f19439aba5ce038b468ebe89bb33c63870c444c5994434269","body":{"detail":"open (98-107) and end_all (129-136) each write the store and then the in-memory map, with no lock held across both, and store calls run on a pool. Interleaved, a session can be live in the store but missing from memory (dead now, back after the next restart), or ended in the store but live in memory (working until the restart). Fix: take the map's write lock before the store call in both, or rebuild the map from live_owner_sessions() after the UPDATE.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":280},"content_hash":"03bd538b96cd0f68e996d7381cccc0d359c2c7e4b523ce645c805732f9f7ccbc"},"summary":"A login redeemed while clax logout runs can leave the store and the in-memory session map disagreeing","supersedes":"d453e0dfcd722f46d65a7512fd7763e2c099c55a3b84aab550a54b72a87156cb","tags":["review","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:55:08.920373Z","id":"68feb8fdd638c4acba18cb150ce3c12f368a7e5358ab261743eb1b3f7ef6239c","body":{"detail":"The lines the detail names (open 98-107, end_all 129-136) are now OwnerSessions::open (crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs:180), end (:259) and end_all (:274). Each takes the writes mutex (OwnerSessions::writing) before its store call and holds it across the map change, as the record's first fix suggests; retire (:224) does the same. That landed in 5ecbdf9bc. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-http:all passes local_trust::tests::a_login_racing_a_logout_leaves_the_store_and_the_map_agreeing (200 rounds of a concurrent open and end_all, comparing Store::live_owner_sessions with the map after each). As reply c6bc2572 says, that test also passed with the lock removed, so the evidence is the structure, not the test. This record was neither written nor fixed by this session (it re-anchored it as dfbaf0bb), so the close is the owner's.","kind":"comment","references":"dfbaf0bbe44f599f19439aba5ce038b468ebe89bb33c63870c444c5994434269","summary":"Holds as fixed at the current lines; proposing the owner close it","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:55:08.920796Z","id":"649717b12b4baef9cfd6f3dc6dec61a6b14c99c72b3721a294d6d2046c5768e4","body":{"detail":"local_trust::gate admits a request whose clax_viewer cookie names a viewer row. Viewers that GET /api/viewers/me minted for any loopback browser before the login existed keep their cookies, so a request carrying one comments, resolves and sends threads to agents as that viewer (never with owner power). A process of the owner's OS user that reads a browser's cookie jar has them, which is the residue the waiver on crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs (Identity::quick_caller) records. No new such viewer is minted: the gate refuses GET /api/viewers/me with no credential, so the set only shrinks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":906},"end":{"line":915},"content_hash":"e3374226978af713e191cd3fdbbcfb93345660ec26ad6754aa5505c1edffa282"},"suggested_fix":"Forget the cookies of local viewers that are neither the owner nor a person in a later migration, once nothing relies on them.","summary":"A clax_viewer cookie minted before the browser login passes the local gate at a viewer's level","supersedes":"090b24064b787c9ccf07c0053c676c0d703e0c58669b256d9aa7610bcddacbb6","tags":["security","local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:55:09.020741Z","id":"bc4f6d64b8c9821a9de9cc8095c317c7badf68b975d17d968dae8e449c9fdc63","body":{"detail":"Failure: a server on another port of the daemon's host (cookies ignore ports) sets, for the daemon's host, MAX_SESSION_COOKIES (8) or more session-shaped clax_owner_<port> values on paths longer than / (the browser sends them before the real one), or enough cookie bytes that the browser's Cookie header passes the server's header limit. live_session reads only the first 8 shaped values of each cookie name, so the real session's cookie is never looked at; or the request is refused before routing. Every request is then the cold browser's, and a clax open does not help, since the planted cookies outlive the login's new one on the same paths. What it grants: nothing. The planted values name no session the attacker can prove, and the proof never leaves the daemon's origin. Recovery: clax logout (which also ends the sessions), or clearing the site's cookies in the browser. Accepted because the cap is what bounds the work of an unauthenticated request (local_trust.rs an_oversized_request_costs_a_bounded_number_of_hashes), and the same attacker can already overwrite the owner cookie for a single request.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":492},"end":{"line":552},"content_hash":"636633dec4b6a2d9afab714b0f2d45120b9445fc256db6983c39fe9343e31818"},"summary":"A server on another port can still deny the owner's browser its session by planting cookies: it grants nothing, survives clax open, and clax logout or clearing the site's cookies recovers","tags":["security","local-trust","revisit:a report of an owner locked out this way, or a cookie scheme the browser scopes to the port (none exists today)","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T03:31:22.736738Z","id":"945745bdd2bc5f931778dbd8a9e08c602fdfbc1b37c5c9e7802415ed68747ffc","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"dcff8e122b054abfeb7339b1d9b3dcebc06849fd27ae9739bc67e9c53776f00f","summary":"Commit f98b779d2 cited by this close was re-signed as 4a96525d2 (same tree, author and message).","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
